    <!-- ★ config_mainDisplayShape is deliberately NOT carried over from the
         stock vendor RRO, even though that RRO does set it. Decoded, stock's
         value is

             M20 0 h1040 s20 0 20 20 v2360 s0 20 -20 20 h-1040 s-20 0 -20 -20 v-2360 ...

         i.e. a rounded rectangle 20+1040+20 = 1080 wide and 20+2360+20 = 2400
         tall. This panel is 2190x3504. The path is for some other model that
         shares Lenovo's vendor image — the same pattern as the
         vendor.lenovo.hardware.vibrator_dual-service entry in stock's
         file_contexts, whose binary does not exist on this device either.

         Copying it would tell every app calling WindowInsets#getDisplayShape()
         that the screen is 1080x2400. AOSP's default is the empty string, which
         makes DisplayShape.fromResources() synthesise the shape from the real
         display size and the rounded_corner_radius above — correct here, and
         correct on any future panel. Leaving it unset is the right answer, not
         an omission. -->

