         properties in the XML are required, because LogicalDisplayMapper
         branches on a feature flag and reads a different one on each side:
         shouldDeviceBeWoken / shouldDeviceBePutToSleep (:642-700) use the
         properties when mDeviceStateManagerFlags.deviceStatePropertyMigration()
         is on and these arrays when it is not. Setting only one half works
         until the flag flips.

         AOSP's defaults are both empty (core/res/res/values/config.xml:731,740),
         which is why the folio does nothing today. -->
    <integer-array name="config_deviceStatesOnWhichToWakeUp">
        <item>0</item>
    </integer-array>
    <integer-array name="config_deviceStatesOnWhichToSleep">
        <item>1</item>
    </integer-array>

